# FinnOS application registry
#
# The catalogue of apps the OS knows about. It ships with the OS and says what
# each app is called, what it looks like and what runs it — never whether it
# is on this machine. That belongs to the package manager, which keeps its
# own list in /var/lib/finn/installed.
#
# Format: id | Name | icon | command | note | source
#
#   id       the name the rest of the system uses
#   Name     what the user sees
#   icon     an SVG in /usr/share/finn/icons
#   command  what to run when the app is launched
#   note     free text, shown as the app's detail line
#   source   catalogue origin: (empty) native, flatpak, winget

settings | Settings | settings-app.svg | /usr/local/bin/finn-settings | Settings
files | Finn Files | files.svg | /usr/local/bin/finn-files | File manager
